{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Amazon Bedrock increases default quotas for Anthropic’s Claude Sonnet 4.5 model in AWS GovCloud (US) - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock, a service offered by AWS, has raised the default quotas for Anthropic's Claude Sonnet 4.5 model in AWS GovCloud (US-West) and AWS GovCloud (US-East) regions. The new quotas are set at 5,000,000 tokens per minute and 1,000 requests per minute, which is a significant 25x increase from the previous limits. This enhancement allows users to efficiently scale their AI workloads in regulated environments. Claude Sonnet 4.5 is Anthropic's latest Sonnet model, known for its proficiency in constructing intricate agents, coding, and long-term tasks while maintaining optimal speed and cost-effectiveness for high-volume applications. To begin using Claude Sonnet 4.5 in Amazon Bedrock, consult the News Blog, AWS GovCloud (US) console, Anthropic's Claude in Amazon Bedrock product page, and the Amazon Bedrock pricing page","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/02/amazon-bedrock-s4.5-quota-aws-govcloud-us/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Amazon Bedrock increases default quotas for Anthropic’s Claude Sonnet 4.5 model in AWS GovCloud (US) - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock has raised the default quotas for Anthropic's Claude Sonnet 4.5 model in AWS GovCloud (US-West) and AWS GovCloud (US-East) to 5,000,000 tokens per minute and 1,000 requests per minute. This enhancement aligns the quotas with commercial AWS regions and allows for more effective scaling of AI workloads in regulated environments. Claude Sonnet 4.5 is Anthropic's latest Sonnet model, which excels at constructing complex agents, coding, and long-horizon tasks while maintaining optimal speed and cost-efficiency for high-volume use-cases. To begin using Claude Sonnet 4.5 in Amazon Bedrock, consult the News Blog, AWS GovCloud (US) console, Anthropic's Claude in Amazon Bedrock product page, and the Amazon Bedrock pricing page","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/02/amazon-bedrock-increases-default-sonnet-4.5-quotas-aws-govcloud-us/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"amazon-bedrock","skill_description":"Builds generative AI applications on Amazon Bedrock. Covers model invocation (Converse API, InvokeModel), RAG with Knowledge Bases, Bedrock Agents, Guardrails, and AgentCore (including the Harness managed agent loop). Applies when invoking models, setting up or migrating Knowledge Bases to Managed, deploying to AgentCore, migrating/porting/converting a Bedrock Agent (including inline agents) to an AgentCore Harness, troubleshooting Bedrock errors (ThrottlingException, AccessDeniedException), or choosing Bedrock models (Claude, Llama, Nova, Titan). Also for prompt caching, quota and throttling diagnosis, cost tracking, migrating between Claude model generations, chunking strategies, and Bedrock model selection. Covers AgentCore Payments (x402, microtransactions, Payment Manager, Connector, Instrument, Coinbase CDP, Stripe Privy, paid endpoints, agent payments). NOT for custom model training, Rekognition, or Comprehend. For SageMaker model discovery, customization, or endpoints, use aws-ai-ml.\n\nServices: bedrock, bedrock-runtime, bedrock-mantle, bedrock-agent, bedrock-agent-runtime, bedrock-agentcore-control, bedrock-agentcore\nTasks: deploy, debug, optimize, design, migrate\nPersona: developer, devops, architect\nWorkload: generative-ai, rag, agents","skill_name":"amazon-bedrock"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"aws-ai-ml","skill_description":"Selects, deploys, and customizes AI models on Amazon SageMaker. Training or Processing jobs, fine-tuning (SFT/DPO/RLVR/RLAIF), model selection, evaluation, SageMaker or Bedrock deployment, inference optimization and endpoint diagnostics. Use when fine-tuning models on SageMaker, choosing a base model to customize or deploy from SageMaker JumpStart or Hub, SageMakerPublicHub, or the model catalog, checking data quality (duplicates, languages, PII), transforming or validating data (reformat, clean, filter, dedupe, split, merge, redact), generating synthetic data, labeling data with a model, human review or annotation and applying its corrections, evaluating model quality, deploying or optimizing endpoints, configuring IAM/S3, or managing SageMaker Managed MLflow. Use for endpoint health, latency, logs, metrics, errors. Covers Serverless Model Customization, Nova and OSS deployment paths, and PySDK v3. NOT for SageMaker Ground Truth labeling jobs, Feature Store, or general AWS infrastructure.\n\nServices: sagemaker, s3, iam, bedrock\nTasks: build, deploy, debug, optimize\nPersona: developer, data-scientist\nWorkload: ai-ml","skill_name":"aws-ai-ml"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"redshift-guide","skill_description":"Amazon Redshift is NOT PostgreSQL; corrects LLM mistakes; covers SQL, metadata, connectivity/auth, storage, query performance, and operations. Applies ONLY to Redshift (provisioned or Serverless). Pushes back on: CREATE INDEX, string_agg, pg_catalog, text type, SERIAL, stl_query. Triggers on: Redshift SQL, Redshift CREATE TABLE, Redshift COPY/UNLOAD, slow or suddenly slow Redshift query, EXPLAIN plan, queue wait, stale statistics/ANALYZE, result cache, Redshift permission denied, Redshift disk full, storage growth, snapshot/backup cost, ghost rows/bloat, VACUUM, spill to disk, distribution skew, Redshift system views, QUALIFY, PIVOT, MERGE, materialized views, Redshift Data API (Python/boto3), Redshift workload management (WLM), concurrency scaling, Redshift resize, Spectrum, awsdatacatalog, connection failures (SSL/TLS, ODBC/JDBC, connection limit), IAM/SAML federation, IAM Identity Center, datashares. Does NOT apply to: S3 policies, Athena, Glue/Iceberg outside Redshift, Aurora, RDS, DynamoDB.\n\nServices: redshift, redshift-serverless, redshift-data-api\nTasks: query, debug, optimize\nPersona: developer, data-engineer, database-administrator, data-analyst\nWorkload: data-warehouse, analytics, etl\n*","skill_name":"redshift-guide"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Check burndown rate for Claude Sonnet 5 on Bedrock"}
